{"content":[{"c":["LINUS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Christian at Rome who joined Paul in sending salutations to Timothy (",{"href":"?bref=2Tim.4.21","r":"2Tim.4.21","rawR":"2Tim.4.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Tim.4.21","value":"2Tim.4.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Tm 4:21"},"). According to Irenaeus and Eusebius, the apostles Peter and Paul made a man named Linus bishop of Rome. Eusebius identified him with the Linus referred to by Paul at the end of 2 Timothy and said that he served for 12 years. The ",{"c":["Apostolic Constitutions,"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," along with other early church documents, also makes this identification."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Linus","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Tm 4:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Tim.4.21","rawQueryValue":"2Tim.4.21","sourceRefExact":"2Tim.4.21"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a227a30eaf0fa1a2f0d7d00726630a8882426eb1c6a37bdcd9ea7390d9a2c9a6","sourceItemName":"Linus","sourceItemOrder":106,"sourceMember":"Articles/L.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Linus","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Linus","title":"Linus","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}